%T A402547 1234531,1394611,3574411,14669251,39803611,102808099,152130091,
%U A402547 162198019,162198019,505313251,505313251,505313251,5273095699,24863186371,24943958491,38816991931,38816991931,257057640739
%N A402547 Least number congruent to 3 modulo 8 that is a quadratic residue modulo the first n odd primes.
%C A402547 Let N = A102476(n+2) be the least modulus with 2^(n+2) square roots of 1. a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402503(n+1) = (N/4 + 1 or 3*N/4 + 1) == 7 (mod 8), or the least m coprime to N such that A402503(n+1)/m is a square modulo N. Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402547 For each n, while a(n) is a square in R and in Q_p for 3 <= p <= prime(n+1), Q_2 is a witness of a(n) being a nonsquare (i.e., a(n) is not a (local) square in Q_2). Sequences -A045535, A401305, A401356, and A402507 are similar constructions (see A401305).
%C A402547 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if D == 4 (mod 8) or D == 8 (mod 32).
%e A402547 The cosets of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402503(n+1), with N = A102476(n+2) for n=0..4:
%e A402547   {3}
%e A402547   {19}
%e A402547   {19, 91}
%e A402547   {211, 331, 379, 499, 571, 739}
%e A402547   {331, 379, 499, 1171, 1219, 1411, 2011, 2179, 2731, 3019, 3259, 3859, 3931, 4579, 5251, 5371, 5611, 5779, 6451, 6931, 7099, 7219, 7291, 7459, 7771, 7891, 8299, 8611, 8779, 9139}
%o A402547 (PARI) a(n) = A401305(n, 3) \\ see A401305 for its program; st == 3 (mod 8) allows to calculate a(n) if a(n-1) is known
%Y A402547 Cf. A102476, A402503.
%Y A402547 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402547 nonn,new
%O A402547 0,1
